# Phase file archive (pipeline close-out)

When a **phase detail file** is **fully Done** (entire letter track: no open Sequence/hold rows for that detail file + Last DoD executed):

## When NOT to archive

- **Subphase** close-out (e.g. C25) does **not** move the parent `phaseC-shell.md` while other C-track items remain open.
- Archive only the **whole** `phaseX-*.md` when that letter track is finished.

## Move (do not delete)

1. Move `docs/todo/phaseX-*.md` → `docs/todo/_archive/phaseX-*.md`.
2. Create `docs/todo/_archive/` if missing.
3. **Do not** keep a second copy in `docs/todo/` (active tree = open phases + `pipeline.md` only).

## Update pipeline

1. Add / update **Done** row in `docs/todo/pipeline.md` with pointer to **`_archive/<file>`**.
2. Remove the item from **Sequence** (renumber if needed).
3. In the **Detail files** affinity table, link archived letters to `_archive/` (or note "archived" with link).

## Trim archived file

Per User Rule phase close-out: status **Done**, shipped summary, pointers to product docs under `docs/` (outside `todo/`); strip queued work.

## Tell the operator

List which files were moved to `_archive/` in the close-out message (no "move it offline yourself").

## Repo-specific paths

| Repo | Active phases | Archive folder |
|---|---|---|
| **wanos-pcb**, **wanos** | `docs/todo/phase*.md` | `docs/todo/_archive/` |
| **hofmans.be** | `docs/phase*.md` | `docs/_archive/` |

On **hofmans.be**, pipeline lives at `docs/pipeline.md` (not under `todo/`).

## Conflicts

User Rule **Phase / ship docs close-out** still requires product-doc audit. This rule replaces "operator manually moves offline" with **in-repo `_archive/`**.
